# Release handoff

This compact screen exercises the complete widget model. Use **Tab** to move
between controls; arrows choose a channel, **Enter** confirms it, and
**Ctrl+Enter** leaves the multiline field. The fields live in a `:::form`, so
**Queue deployment** validates them first and reports one `submit` event
instead of a `click`.

::::form{id="handoff" label="Deployment request"}

:::radio{id="channel" value="staging"}
::option{value="canary" label="Canary · 5% traffic"}
::option{value="staging" label="Staging · internal verification"}
::option{value="production" label="Production · full rollout"}
:::

::input{id="owner" label="Release owner" value="Ada" required}

::input{id="ticket" label="Tracking ticket" placeholder="REL-1234" pattern="[A-Z]+-[0-9]+" required}

::input{id="token" label="Rollback token" mask minLength="12"}

::textarea{id="notes" label="Release notes" placeholder="Risks, checks, and rollback plan…" rows="3" maxLength="500"}

::checkbox{id="approved" label="All pre-flight checks passed"}

::button{id="deploy" label="Queue deployment" submit}

::::

Clear **Release owner** and try again to see the error rows appear — they show
up only after a failed submit and clear as soon as you edit the field. The
rollback token is masked on screen (`•` per character) but reaches the host
intact in the `submit` values.
